      "The chain fails quietly. A vaccine that has been too warm usually looks exactly the same as one that has not, so a clinic can administer a useless dose and nobody involved will know.",
      "A simple device addresses this. A vial monitor is a small square of heat-sensitive material printed on the label, and it darkens cumulatively with exposure, so a health worker can read the dose's history before using it.",
