      "Shading makes this worse. A solid colour over a district implies uniform control. A government holding the towns while someone else moves between them cannot be drawn that way honestly.",
      "Names carry a position too. A town with two names in two languages must be labelled somehow. Whichever is chosen is read as a claim, even when the mapmaker meant only to be understood.",
