      "Material can also move. Burrowing animals, roots and later digging carry small objects down through a sequence. A sample can come from a layer it was never deposited in.",
      "Calibration adds a step. Radiocarbon years are not calendar years. Converting uses a curve built from tree rings. The curve has flat stretches where one measurement covers several centuries.",
      "So the first question is what each date dated. A disagreement between the death of a tree and the position of a layer is not a disagreement about when people were there.",
      "Where that does not settle it, the conflict is real. More samples usually resolve it. Several dates from several materials in several layers constrain a sequence as one measurement cannot.",
